+# v30 — centre-start map dragging and portal restriction removed
+
+Every fixed-route stroke starts at reference pixel (285,530), near the map
+centre. Direction is centre minus the next target's measured screen position.
+For a target below and to the right, the mouse moves quickly up and left.
+The button stays held between movement and screenshot checks. A stroke keeps
+its initial direction, checks at most every 240 reference pixels, and stops
+at the first verified frame with the target available. It does not need
+per-location measurements or a fixed desktop window size.
+
+Cursor paths use the four exact marked title, legend, zoom/portrait and bottom
+control exclusions. Their coordinates are unchanged from v29. No padding is
+added. The cursor stops at the first excluded pixel or viewport edge. A longer
+transition releases at rest and starts another hold from the centre.
+
+The 0.18-second stationary release pause and fresh position verification remain.
+Windows button state is checked before held movement. If the button has been
+released, input stops before another cursor movement. This detects a lost
+Windows hold; it cannot prove how BlueStacks handles a delivered gesture.
+
+Fixed-route alignment recovery no longer sends the old blind reverse sweeps.
+It attempts fresh recognition in place, then stops with checked locations kept
+if it cannot establish the position. Legacy automatic-planner recovery is
+unchanged; the Gem Sniping saved-route path uses the fixed-route policy.
+
+All known-portal coordinate filtering, the runtime stop and editor portal
+warning are removed from application code. This includes the rebuilt EXE.
+Hide portal icons in the game's map filter as requested. The default route
+coordinates, route exclusions, saved profiles, point removal, detector and
+inspection settings are retained. Removed points are not runtime lock checks.
+
+The app header shows v30, including when run from the rebuilt EXE. Start and
+drag diagnostics are recorded locally in the existing loonglens.log.
+
+Exit the old app completely, extract the full folder and run its LoongLens.exe.
+Python edits affect RUN_LOONG_LENS.bat, while the EXE contains its own code.
+The launcher activates an existing instance, so exit it before switching.
+Settings, routes and history remain in %LOCALAPPDATA%\LoongLens.
+
+Windows checks cover the frozen GUI, icon, resources, held input and F10 on the
+app's own test window. Route tests and timings use simulated map delivery and
+atlas screenshots. They do not establish live BlueStacks timing or reproduce
+the exact state of the user's intermittent Celestship/XIV failure.
